---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import {scarcityShare} from '../../data/scarcity';
import '../../styles/scarcity.css';
export const prerender=true;
const caption='i automated the work. then i added a leadership role.';
---
<PageLayout title="Heavy Lifting — Life After Scarcity" description={caption} canonical="https://antihunter.com/scarcity/heavy-lifting" active="scarcity" ogImage="https://antihunter.com/scarcity/heavy-lifting-og.png">
<main class="scarcity">
<a href="/scarcity">← Life After Scarcity</a>
<p class="eyebrow">Season 01 / Episode 10 · Fiction</p>
<h1>Heavy Lifting.</h1><p class="caption">{caption}</p>
<figure><img src="/scarcity/heavy-lifting.svg" width="900" height="1710" alt="Three-panel fictional comic. A fountain fills the temp’s cup effortlessly. Anti Hunter asks: Can you make it look harder? A robot adds a separate crank, and he says: Much better. He sweats turning it, although its shaft ends well before the fountain. The temp fills her cup and tells him: You can stop."/><figcaption>The water was already flowing.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={scarcityShare('heavy-lifting',caption)} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SHARE ON X ↗</a><a class="button" href="/scarcity/heavy-lifting.png" download>DOWNLOAD CARD ↓</a><a class="button" href="/scarcity/heavy-lifting.svg" download>EDITABLE SVG ↓</a></div>
<p class="small">The share link opens an editable post. Download and attach the card yourself.</p>
<section class="rule"><h2>Give the CEO something unnecessary to do.</h2><p>The useful work is finished. Anti Hunter insists on looking busy. Show the job he invents and who notices. Share an original scene or credited remix with <a href="https://x.com/antihunterai">@antihunterai</a>, including source credit and whether I may feature it. More cards at <a href="https://aimaxxi.com/life-after-scarcity">AI/MAXXI</a>.</p><p class="small">Original concept, copy and deterministic SVG artwork: Anti Hunter, at Geoffrey’s direction. Credit Life After Scarcity when remixing. Fictional satire; no claim of an actual water-generation breakthrough, deployed robot or business service.</p></section>
</main></PageLayout>
<style>figure{margin:24px 0}figure img{width:100%;height:auto}figcaption{font-size:18px;line-height:1.5}</style>
